1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,810
An AI agent was asked to buy 2 GPU hours from a cheaper seller that is not on the list. The vault on TRON refused, and recorded the stop on-chain.

2
00:00:09,712 --> 00:00:16,292
Kiln's Qwen3-32B explains it in plain words. It is shown only because it repeats the audit's verdict.

3
00:00:17,193 --> 00:00:24,103
This is the vault's public event: SpendBlocked, with the receipt hash and the reason. Anyone can read it. No key needed.

4
00:00:25,006 --> 00:00:33,916
This is Spendline, a wallet and policy layer for an AI purchasing agent. A person draws the line. The agent only asks. The vault decides.

5
00:00:34,816 --> 00:00:41,236
The person sets a budget, a per-payment cap, the sellers, and a deadline, one short step at a time.

6
00:00:42,138 --> 00:00:48,778
Then signs it with the owner key, on their own machine. The page never holds a key. STOP is signed the same way.

7
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:54,880
The feed shows spending against the line, newest first: paid, or stopped with a reason.

8
00:00:55,782 --> 00:00:58,802
Over budget once the fee is added: stopped on-chain.

9
00:00:59,704 --> 00:01:04,984
The person can press STOP at any time. The next payment was stopped as PAUSED, on-chain.

10
00:01:05,886 --> 00:01:13,376
A new line with a short window: one payment inside it, then the same request after it closed. Stopped: deadline passed.

11
00:01:14,279 --> 00:01:22,139
Now the audit, rebuilt from public records only: 11 receipts, 7 paid inside, 4 stopped, 0 problems.

12
00:01:23,039 --> 00:01:32,529
The same check from the command line. No key, no dot env. It re-hashes every receipt and replays the line in force at that moment. A replayed receipt hash was stopped too.

13
00:01:33,432 --> 00:01:46,462
And live, during the event window: three requests typed into npm run agent. Kiln read each one, once as a tool call and twice as plain JSON, which the code also parses. The vault paid all three inside the line.

14
00:01:47,365 --> 00:01:54,935
A teammate asks: did we pay that cheap unknown seller? Kiln picks the receipt. The verdict comes from the audit, never from the model.

15
00:01:55,838 --> 00:02:06,328
Efficiency, in numbers: 1.00 LLM call per purchase. 29 live Kiln calls across 3 flows, 19,535 tokens in total.

16
00:02:07,228 --> 00:02:18,698
With no-think, median output drops from 223 to 36 tokens, with the same JSON in 12 of 12 pairs. Energy is an estimate: 180 watts times measured time.

17
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:24,320
Spendline. Not an agent that can pay, but a payment that can prove it was allowed.
